  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations to Utah totaled $4.6B in FY2026 to date, across 7,174 awards with an average award size of $647K. Obligations fell 11.2% year over year. The Department of Defense dominates buying in the state, accounting for $3.6B of obligations. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the single largest industry by dollars, with $2.5B in obligations, and NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP is the largest vendor at $2.5B. Other notable buyers include the Department of the Treasury with $391M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $112M. Outside defense, the top industries include Nonferrous Metal Rolling, Drawing, and Extruding at $364M and Engineering Services at $193M. Top vendors beyond Northrop Grumman include ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $363M and L3 TECHNOLOGIES, INC. at $227M. Year-to-date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress, so cumulative FY2026 to date figures may change as the year closes.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the FY2026 to date spending pattern in Utah?",
        "body": "Defense work drives the FY2026 to date totals: the Department of Defense is responsible for $3.6B of the $4.6B in obligations. Large awards in Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing and major payments to NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP at $2.5B concentrate dollars in a few programs. Nondefense agencies such as the Department of the Treasury ($391M) and the Department of Veterans Affairs ($112M) contribute meaningful but much smaller shares."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are obligations across vendors and industries?",
        "body": "Obligations are highly concentrated: Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for $2.5B and NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP also accounts for $2.5B. The next largest industry and vendors drop to the hundreds of millions, for example Nonferrous Metal Rolling, Drawing, and Extruding at $364M and ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $363M. The top buying agency, the Department of Defense, holds the largest single-agency share at $3.6B."
      }
    ]
  },
